BT 1 0 0 1 0 30 Tm 13.2 TL /F1 9.6 Tf 0 0 0 rg (A string cannot be modified in place, so ) Tj /F4 9.6 Tf (text += p) Tj /F1 9.6 Tf ( conceptually builds a brand-new string and copies every) Tj T* (old character into it on each pass. For n lines this copies on the order of n) Tj /F1 7.68 Tf 4.8 Ts (2) Tj /F1 9.6 Tf 0 Ts ( characters in total, i.e. O\(n) Tj /F1 7.68 Tf 4.8 Ts (2) Tj /F1 9.6 Tf 0 Ts (\). ) Tj /F4 9.6 Tf (join) Tj /F1 9.6 Tf  T* (first works out the total size, allocates once and copies each piece once, which is O\(n\).) Tj T* ET
