BT 1 0 0 1 0 56.4 Tm 13.2 TL /F2 9.6 Tf 0 0 0 rg (The CPython caveat.) Tj /F1 9.6 Tf ( CPython sometimes optimises ) Tj /F4 9.6 Tf (+=) Tj /F1 9.6 Tf (: if nothing else references the string, it can resize it in) Tj T* (place, so ) Tj /F4 9.6 Tf (+=) Tj /F1 9.6 Tf ( looks close to linear in a simple loop like this one and the measured gap can be small. That is an) Tj T* (implementation detail, not a language guarantee: it does not apply in other interpreters, nor when the string is) Tj T* (also referenced elsewhere \(for example ) Tj /F4 9.6 Tf (self.text += ...) Tj /F1 9.6 Tf (\). ) Tj /F4 9.6 Tf (join\(\)) Tj /F1 9.6 Tf ( is guaranteed linear everywhere, so it) Tj T* (remains the recommended practice.) Tj T* ET
